            <h2>2. The Blind Relay: What We Can’t See, We Can’t Give Away</h2>
            <p><b>The Advantage:</b> Traditional servers log your IP address and connection times. Our "Blind Relay" doctrine makes the server a mere conduit.</p>
            <ul>
                <li><span class="highlight">Instant IP Discard:</span> The moment you connect, your IP address is processed in volatile RAM and instantly overwritten. No logs. No history. No trail.</li>
                <li><span class="highlight">RAM-to-RAM Delivery:</span> Messages move from your device's memory to the recipient's memory. Once delivered, they are purged from our relay.</li>
                <li><span class="highlight">Zero Knowledge:</span> Because of our "Scorched Metadata" standard, the server doesn't even know the name or type of the file you sent. To us, everything is just unreadable noise.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>3. Forensic Shredding: Beyond Simple Deletion</h2>
            <p><b>The Advantage:</b> On most phones, "deleted" messages stay on the storage chip, waiting for recovery software to find them.</p>
            <ul>
                <li><span class="highlight">Active Decay:</span> When you delete a message in SecureMessenger, we don't just "hide" it. We trigger a forensic-grade overwrite, replacing your data with random noise before purging it from the silicon.</li>
                <li><span class="highlight">Hardware-Anchored Security:</span> Your encryption keys are "trapped" inside your phone’s Hardware Secure Element (TEE). Even if your phone is lost or stolen, your data remains an unbreakable vault.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
